         "SVC behaves as a variable reactive admittance; its maximum reactive current output is proportional to grid voltage: I_max = Y * V. Under severe grid faults where voltage plunges to 0.5 pu, an SVC's reactive power support collapses quadratically: Q = V^2 * Y (producing only 25% of rated VARs).<br>A STATCOM acts as a controllable AC voltage source behind a coupling transformer; it can maintain its full rated reactive capacitive current even at low grid voltages (I_max = I_rated = constant), providing Q propto V support. A STATCOM also occupies ~60% less substation footprint and produces much faster dynamic response (< 10 ms vs 30-40 ms for SVC).",
