         "TRV is caused by high-frequency energy oscillation between the system source inductance L and stray capacitance C: v(t) = V_peak * [1 - cos(t / sqrt(L*C))]. The Rate of Rise of Recovery Voltage is RRRV = dv/dt, with a maximum value of RRRV_max = V_peak / sqrt(L*C).<br>For successful fault clearing, the rate at which the dielectric strength between the parting contacts builds up must exceed RRRV. If RRRV outpaces dielectric recovery, the arc restrikes, maintaining the fault and potentially blowing up the breaker chamber.",
